    "title": "What is the Memento Pattern, and how does it preserve Encapsulation during state restoration?",
    "answer": "The Memento Pattern captures and externalizes an object's internal state without violating encapsulation, allowing the object to be restored to that state later:\n\n3 Roles:\n1. Originator: The object whose state is being tracked (creates memento, restores from memento).\n2. Memento: Passive value object storing the originator's snapshot. Wide interface visible only to Originator; narrow interface exposed to others.\n3. Caretaker: Holds the memento history stack, but never inspects or mutates memento contents.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Captures and restores object state without breaking encapsulation.",
      "Caretaker manages history stack; Originator produces and consumes snapshots.",
      "Essential for savegame systems and multi-step transaction rollbacks."
    ],
