    "title": "Compare the Template Method Pattern with the Strategy Pattern. Which adheres better to the Open/Closed Principle?",
    "answer": "1. Mechanism:\n   - Template Method uses Inheritance. An abstract base class defines the skeleton/algorithm steps in a `final` method and provides hook or abstract methods for subclasses to override specific steps.\n   - Strategy uses Composition. The context class delegates an entire algorithm to an injected strategy interface.\n\n2. Granularity:\n   - Template Method controls the fine-grained flow and order of execution; subclasses only fill in the blanks.\n   - Strategy allows swapping out the entire algorithm wholesale.\n\n3. SOLID Adherence (Open/Closed & Composition):\n   - Strategy adheres better to OOP principles because it favors composition over inheritance. Inheritance introduces tight compile-time coupling with the base class.\n   - Template method can be dangerous if the base class changes its algorithm flow, inadvertently breaking subclasses (Fragile Base Class problem).",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Template Method: Inheritance-based; base class defines algorithm structure via a final method.",
      "Strategy: Composition-based; algorithm interface injected at runtime.",
      "Strategy offers greater runtime flexibility and looser coupling than Template Method."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "java",
      "code": "```java\n// Template Method Pattern\nabstract class DataParser {\n    // Template method defining algorithm invariant sequence\n    public final void process() {\n        readData();\n        parse();\n        saveToDatabase();\n    }\n    abstract void readData();\n    abstract void parse();\n    void saveToDatabase() { System.out.println(\"Saved to SQL\"); } // Default hook\n}\n\nclass CSVParser extends DataParser {\n    void readData() { System.out.println(\"Reading CSV file\"); }\n    void parse() { System.out.println(\"Parsing CSV rows\"); }\n}\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "`HttpServlet.service()` in Java EE is a classic Template Method: it parses the request and invokes `doGet()` or `doPost()`, which developers override.",
