    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "OOPS",
    "subject_label": "OOPs",
    "title": "Describe the God Object, Shotgun Surgery, and Divergent Change code smells. How do you refactor them?",
    "answer": "1. God Object (Monolithic Class):\n   - A class that knows too much or does too much, accumulating thousands of lines of code and dozens of unrelated responsibilities.\n   - Refactor: Apply Single Responsibility Principle. Extract cohesive sub-classes and delegate duties.\n\n2. Divergent Change:\n   - One class is commonly changed in different ways for different reasons. (e.g., modifying `Order` when database schema changes, and ALSO when tax calculation rules change).\n   - Refactor: Extract classes so each class changes for only ONE distinct business reason.\n\n3. Shotgun Surgery:\n   - The opposite of Divergent Change: Making one single conceptual change requires making small, scattered edits across dozens of different classes.\n   - Causes: High coupling and fragmented business logic.\n   - Refactor: Move scattered methods and fields into a single unified class (Move Method / Move Field).",
    "bullet_points": [
      "God Object: One giant class holding all application state and logic.",
      "Divergent Change: One class altered by many unrelated business requirement changes.",
      "Shotgun Surgery: One business requirement change forces edits across many classes."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "java",
      "code": "```java\n// Divergent Change: Order altered for Tax rules, DB logic, and PDF formatting\nclass Order {\n    void calculateVAT() { /* Tax logic */ }\n    void saveToPostgres() { /* DB logic */ }\n    void generateInvoicePDF() { /* Presentation logic */ }\n}\n\n// Refactored via SRP:\nclass OrderTaxCalculator { double calculateVAT(Order o) { /*...*/ } }\nclass OrderRepository { void save(Order o) { /*...*/ } }\nclass InvoicePdfGenerator { byte[] generate(Order o) { /*...*/ } }\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "Remember the mnemonic: Divergent Change = 1 class, many reasons to change. Shotgun Surgery = 1 reason, many classes to change.",
