    "topic_id": "topic-oops",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "OOPS",
    "subject_label": "OOPs",
    "title": "What is Reflection in OOP, and what are its major performance, security, and architectural drawbacks?",
    "answer": "Reflection is an OOP language capability that allows a program to inspect, introspect, and modify its own internal structure, classes, fields, and methods at runtime.\n\nKey Use Cases:\n- Dependency Injection frameworks (Spring, Guice) wiring objects.\n- Object-Relational Mappers (Hibernate) mapping SQL rows to private fields.\n- Serialization libraries (Jackson, Gson) converting JSON to POJOs.\n\nDrawbacks:\n1. Performance Overhead: Reflective method invocations bypass JIT compiler optimizations (like method inlining) and incur dynamic argument boxing/unboxing and type verification checks.\n2. Breaks Encapsulation: `field.setAccessible(true)` can inspect and mutate private, final fields, subverting immutability guarantees.\n3. Runtime Failure vs Compile-time Safety: Method name typos or signature mismatches fail at runtime with `NoSuchMethodException` rather than compile-time errors.\n4. Security Manager & GraalVM Native Image barriers: Reflection requires special reflection configuration files for Ahead-Of-Time (AOT) compilation.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Reflection allows runtime inspection and mutation of classes, fields, and constructors.",
      "Disables JIT compiler inlining and adds heavy runtime dynamic dispatch overhead.",
      "Breaks encapsulation by granting access to private and final fields."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "java",
      "code": "```java\n// Reflectively accessing private field\npublic class SecretVault {\n    private final String secretKey = \"SUPER_SECRET\";\n}\n\n// Client bypassing encapsulation:\nSecretVault vault = new SecretVault();\nField field = SecretVault.class.getDeclaredField(\"secretKey\");\nfield.setAccessible(true); // Suppresses Java language access checks!\nString value = (String) field.get(vault);\nSystem.out.println(\"Extracted secret: \" + value);\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "Modern frameworks are increasingly shifting from runtime reflection to compile-time annotation processing (e.g., Dagger 2, Micronaut, MapStruct) for zero-overhead performance.",
