    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "OOPS",
    "subject_label": "OOPs",
    "title": "What is the Visitor Pattern and how does it emulate Double Dispatch in single-dispatch languages like Java/C++?",
    "answer": "Single-dispatch languages (Java, C++, C#) select which method to execute at runtime based solely on ONE receiver type (the object before the dot: `obj.method()`). The static compile-time type of the method argument determines which overload to call.\n\nDouble Dispatch is the ability to choose a method based on the runtime types of TWO objects (the receiver AND the argument).\n\nThe Visitor Pattern solves this by performing two single-dispatch calls in succession:\n1. First Dispatch: Client calls `element.accept(visitor)`. Runtime polymorphism dispatches to the concrete element class (`Circle.accept(Visitor v)`).\n2. Second Dispatch: Inside `accept`, the concrete element invokes `visitor.visit(this)`. Because `this` is statically known to be `Circle`, the compiler binds to `visit(Circle c)`.\n\nBenefit: You can add new operations (e.g., ExportToXMLVisitor, RenderSVGVisitor) to an existing object hierarchy without modifying any of the element classes!",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Emulates double dispatch by combining two single polymorphic dispatches.",
      "Allows adding new operations to existing class hierarchies without modifying them.",
      "Widely used in AST (Abstract Syntax Tree) compilers and document processing engines."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "java",
      "code": "```java\ninterface Visitor {\n    void visit(Book b);\n    void visit(Fruit f);\n}\n\ninterface ItemElement {\n    void accept(Visitor v);\n}\n\nclass Book implements ItemElement {\n    public void accept(Visitor v) { v.visit(this); } // 'this' binds to Book!\n}\n\nclass ShoppingCartVisitor implements Visitor {\n    public void visit(Book b) { System.out.println(\"Processing book discount\"); }\n    public void visit(Fruit f) { System.out.println(\"Processing fruit weight\"); }\n}\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "The major drawback of Visitor is that adding a NEW element class requires updating the Visitor interface and all concrete visitor implementations.",
