    "title": "Design a Low-Level Object-Oriented Architecture for a Multi-Floor Parking Lot System.",
    "answer": "In Low-Level Design (LLD) interviews, the Parking Lot is a standard benchmark question to test OOP modeling, polymorphism, and encapsulation.\n\nKey Entities & Relationships:\n1. `Vehicle` (Abstract Base Class): Extended by `Motorcycle`, `Car`, `Bus`. Has license plate and `VehicleSize` enum (`SMALL`, `MEDIUM`, `LARGE`).\n2. `ParkingSpot` (Base Class): Has `spotId`, `isAvailable`, and `SpotType` enum (`MOTORCYCLE`, `COMPACT`, `LARGE`). Method `canFitVehicle(Vehicle v)` uses polymorphic sizing rules.\n3. `ParkingFloor`: Manages collections of parking spots by size. Methods `findAvailableSpot(Vehicle v)`, `parkVehicle()`, `vacateSpot()`.\n4. `ParkingLot` (Singleton): Orchestrates multiple `ParkingFloor` instances, Entry/Exit gates, and ticket dispatch.\n5. `ParkingTicket`: Stores `ticketId`, `spotId`, `entryTime`, and calculates fee on exit using Strategy pattern (`FeeCalculationStrategy`).",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Polymorphic vehicle and spot sizing via enums and inheritance.",
      "ParkingLot as a thread-safe Singleton orchestrating multi-floor collections.",
      "Decouples fee calculation using the Strategy Pattern."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "java",
      "code": "```java\nenum VehicleType { MOTORCYCLE, CAR, BUS }\n\nabstract class Vehicle {\n    private String plate;\n    private VehicleType type;\n    public Vehicle(String p, VehicleType t) { this.plate = p; this.type = t; }\n    public VehicleType getType() { return type; }\n}\n\nclass Car extends Vehicle { public Car(String p) { super(p, VehicleType.CAR); } }\n\nclass ParkingSpot {\n    private int spotNumber;\n    private VehicleType supportedType;\n    private Vehicle currentVehicle;\n\n    public synchronized boolean isAvailable() { return currentVehicle == null; }\n    public synchronized boolean assignVehicle(Vehicle v) {\n        if (!isAvailable() || v.getType() != supportedType) return false;\n        this.currentVehicle = v;\n        return true;\n    }\n    public synchronized void vacate() { this.currentVehicle = null; }\n}\n```"
    },
