    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "OOPS",
    "subject_label": "OOPs",
    "title": "Design an OOP Elevator System. How do you model elevator states, dispatch algorithms, and request queues?",
    "answer": "Elevator System LLD evaluates State Pattern modeling and scheduling algorithms:\n\n1. Entities:\n   - `ElevatorCar`: Holds `currentFloor`, `Direction` (`UP`, `DOWN`, `IDLE`), `ElevatorState` (`MOVING`, `STOPPED`, `DOORS_OPEN`), and internal request queue.\n   - `ElevatorController`: Manages multiple elevator cars, receives external floor requests, and assigns them.\n   - `InternalButton` & `ExternalButton`: Dispatch floor requests to the controller.\n   - `ElevatorState` (State Pattern): `MovingState`, `StoppedState`, `MaintenanceState`.\n\n2. Scheduling Algorithm (SCAN / LOOK / SCAN-like Disk Scheduling):\n   - Maintains two priority queues: `upQueue` (Min-Heap for floors above moving up) and `downQueue` (Max-Heap for floors below moving down).\n   - Continues in the current direction servicing requests until queue is empty, then reverses direction, eliminating starvation.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Models elevator state transitions using the State Pattern.",
      "Uses SCAN/LOOK algorithm with Min-Heap and Max-Heap priority queues.",
      "ElevatorController dispatches Hall Calls to the optimal elevator car based on proximity and direction."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "java",
      "code": "```java\nenum Direction { UP, DOWN, IDLE }\n\nclass ElevatorCar {\n    private int id;\n    private int currentFloor = 0;\n    private Direction direction = Direction.IDLE;\n    private TreeSet<Integer> upStops = new TreeSet<>();\n    private TreeSet<Integer> downStops = new TreeSet<>(Collections.reverseOrder());\n\n    public synchronized void addStop(int targetFloor) {\n        if (targetFloor > currentFloor) upStops.add(targetFloor);\n        else downStops.add(targetFloor);\n        if (direction == Direction.IDLE) {\n            direction = targetFloor > currentFloor ? Direction.UP : Direction.DOWN;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public synchronized void moveStep() {\n        if (direction == Direction.UP) {\n            if (!upStops.isEmpty()) {\n                currentFloor = upStops.pollFirst();\n            } else if (!downStops.isEmpty()) {\n                direction = Direction.DOWN;\n            } else direction = Direction.IDLE;\n        }\n    }\n}\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "When designing elevators, discuss the 'Starvation Problem': how pure proximity dispatch can leave a user waiting forever on an extreme floor without a fair LOOK algorithm.",
