    "id": "int-dbms-014",
    "topic_id": "topic-dbms",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "DBMS",
    "subject_label": "DBMS",
    "title": "What is a Canonical / Minimal Cover of a set of Functional Dependencies, and what is the 3-step algorithm to find it?",
    "answer": "A Canonical Cover $F_c$ of a set of functional dependencies $F$ is a minimal equivalent set of dependencies that has the same closure ($F_c^+ = F^+$) with zero redundancies.\n\nProperties of Minimal Cover:\n1. Every dependency in $F_c$ has a single attribute on its right-hand side ($X \to A$).\n2. No extraneous attributes on the left-hand side (no attribute in $X$ can be deleted without changing $F^+$).\n3. No redundant functional dependencies (no dependency can be removed from $F_c$ without changing $F^+$).\n\n3-Step Algorithm:\n1. Singleton RHS: Decompose all RHS attributes into singletons using decomposition rule ($X \to YZ \\implies X \to Y, X \to Z$).\n2. Remove Extraneous LHS Attributes: For each $X \to A$, if $B \\in X$, compute closure of $(X \\setminus \\{B\\})$ using $F$. If $A \\in (X \\setminus \\{B\\})^+$, then $B$ is extraneous and can be removed from LHS.\n3. Remove Redundant FDs: For each dependency $f: X \to A \\in F$, temporarily remove $f$ from $F$. Compute $X^+$ using $F \\setminus \\{f\\}$. If $A \\in X^+$, then $f$ was redundant; permanently delete it.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Canonical cover has singleton RHS attributes, no extraneous LHS attributes, and no redundant FDs.",
      "Guarantees that database schemas are normalized with the minimum possible number of integrity constraints.",
      "Equivalent to the original set: $F_c^+ = F^+$."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "```text\nExample: F = { A -> BC, B -> C, A -> B, AB -> C }\nStep 1 (Singleton RHS): { A -> B, A -> C, B -> C, A -> B, AB -> C }\nStep 2 (Remove duplicate & extraneous):\n  In AB -> C: since B -> C, A is extraneous in AB -> C -> becomes B -> C.\nStep 3 (Remove redundant FDs):\n  For A -> C: Since A -> B and B -> C, A+ without A -> C still includes C!\n  Therefore A -> C is redundant!\nCanonical Cover Fc = { A -> B, B -> C }\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "Always check for extraneous LHS attributes before checking for redundant FDs; changing the LHS can reveal dependencies that become redundant in step 3.",
    "company_tags": [
      "Google",
      "Amazon",
      "Microsoft",
      "Oracle"
    ],
    "frequency": "HIGH",
    "difficulty": "MEDIUM",
    "is_hidden": false,
    "is_deleted": false,
    "sort_order": 14
