    "id": "int-dbms-032",
    "topic_id": "topic-dbms",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "DBMS",
    "subject_label": "DBMS",
    "title": "How do timestamp-based Deadlock Prevention schemes (Wait-Die vs Wound-Wait) prevent circular wait? Which is preemptive?",
    "answer": "Deadlock prevention schemes avoid deadlocks upfront by assigning each transaction a unique monotonically increasing timestamp $TS(T_i)$ when it starts. Older transactions have smaller timestamps ($TS(T_{old}) < TS(T_{young})$).\n\nWhen transaction $T_i$ requests a lock held by $T_j$:\n\n1. Wait-Die Scheme (Non-preemptive):\n   - If $T_{old}$ requests lock held by $T_{young}$: $T_{old}$ is allowed to WAIT.\n   - If $T_{young}$ requests lock held by $T_{old}$: $T_{young}$ DIES (aborts and restarts with its original timestamp).\n   - Rule: 'Old waits, young dies'. A young transaction can never wait for an older one, so cycles are impossible.\n\n2. Wound-Wait Scheme (Preemptive):\n   - If $T_{old}$ requests lock held by $T_{young}$: $T_{old}$ WOUNDS $T_{young}$ ($T_{young}$ is preempted, aborted, and rolls back, releasing its lock to $T_{old}$).\n   - If $T_{young}$ requests lock held by $T_{old}$: $T_{young}$ is allowed to WAIT.\n   - Rule: 'Old wounds, young waits'.\n\nWound-Wait minimizes aborts compared to Wait-Die because older transactions pre-emptively seize resources rather than dying repeatedly.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Wait-Die is non-preemptive: older transactions wait, younger transactions abort/die.",
      "Wound-Wait is preemptive: older transactions wound/abort younger lock-holders.",
      "Both schemes preserve the original transaction timestamp upon restart to prevent starvation."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "```text\nComparison:\nRequest: Ti requests lock held by Tj\n--------------------------------------------------------------\nScheme     | If Ti is Older (TS(i) < TS(j)) | If Ti is Younger\n--------------------------------------------------------------\nWait-Die   | Ti WAITS                       | Ti DIES (aborts)\nWound-Wait | Ti WOUNDS Tj (Tj aborts)       | Ti WAITS\n--------------------------------------------------------------\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "Starvation Prevention: When an aborted transaction restarts, it must retain its ORIGINAL timestamp; otherwise, an unfortunate transaction could be aborted indefinitely.",
    "company_tags": [
      "Google",
      "Amazon",
      "Microsoft",
      "Meta"
    ],
    "frequency": "VERY_HIGH",
