    "id": "int-dbms-049",
    "topic_id": "topic-dbms",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "DBMS",
    "subject_label": "DBMS",
    "title": "How does the Two-Phase Commit (2PC) protocol achieve atomicity across distributed nodes? Why is 2PC a 'Blocking' protocol?",
    "answer": "The Two-Phase Commit (2PC) protocol coordinates multiple distributed database nodes (participants) to ensure a distributed transaction commits atomically across all nodes or rolls back completely.\n\nTwo Phases:\n1. Phase 1: Prepare Phase:\n   - Coordinator sends `PREPARE` message to all participants.\n   - Each participant executes the transaction locally, writes Undo/Redo logs to disk, acquires locks, and votes:\n     - `VOTE_COMMIT`: Ready to commit.\n     - `VOTE_ABORT`: Failed or conflict detected.\n2. Phase 2: Commit Phase:\n   - If ALL participants voted `VOTE_COMMIT`, Coordinator writes `COMMIT` to its log and broadcasts `GLOBAL_COMMIT`.\n   - If ANY participant voted `VOTE_ABORT` (or timed out), Coordinator broadcasts `GLOBAL_ABORT`.\n   - Participants execute the command, release locks, and reply `ACK`.\n\nWhy 2PC is a 'Blocking' Protocol (Major Vulnerability):\nIf the Coordinator crashes AFTER participants vote `VOTE_COMMIT` but BEFORE broadcasting `GLOBAL_COMMIT`, participants are stuck in limbo! They cannot decide unilaterally to abort (because the coordinator might have decided to commit), and they cannot decide to commit (because another participant might have aborted). They must remain blocked, holding exclusive database locks indefinitely until the coordinator recovers!",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Prepare phase: Participants execute locally, write WAL, and vote commit or abort.",
      "Commit phase: Coordinator broadcasts global commit if all voted yes; global abort otherwise.",
      "Blocking flaw: If coordinator crashes during commit phase, participants remain blocked holding locks."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "```text\nTwo-Phase Commit Flow:\nCoordinator                    Participant 1           Participant 2\n    | --- 1. PREPARE ---------->     |                       |\n    | --- 1. PREPARE --------------------------------------> |\n    | <-- 2. VOTE_COMMIT -------     |                       |\n    | <-- 2. VOTE_COMMIT ----------------------------------- |\n    |\n    | (Coordinator logs COMMIT)\n    |\n    | --- 3. GLOBAL_COMMIT ---->     |                       |\n    | --- 3. GLOBAL_COMMIT --------------------------------> |\n    | <-- 4. ACK ---------------     |                       |\n    | <-- 4. ACK ------------------------------------------- |\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "Three-Phase Commit (3PC) and Paxos/Raft-based consensus engines (Spanner, CockroachDB) were created specifically to eliminate the blocking coordinator failure mode of 2PC.",
    "company_tags": [
      "Google",
      "Amazon",
      "Microsoft",
      "Salesforce"
    ],
    "frequency": "VERY_HIGH",
