    "id": "int-dbms-072",
    "topic_id": "topic-dbms",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "DBMS",
    "subject_label": "DBMS",
    "title": "What is the PostgreSQL Transaction ID (XID) Wraparound problem, and how does `VACUUM FREEZE` prevent catastrophic database shutdown?",
    "answer": "PostgreSQL transaction IDs (`XIDs`) are 32-bit unsigned integers. A 32-bit integer supports approximately 4.29 billion values ($2^{32}$).\n\nThe Wraparound Danger:\n- In PostgreSQL's circular transaction space, comparing two XIDs uses modulo arithmetic: an XID is considered 'in the past' if it is within $2^{31}$ transactions, and 'in the future' otherwise.\n- If a database runs for months without maintenance and consumes 2.1 billion transactions without freezing old IDs, old committed transactions wrap around into the 'future'!\n- Catastrophe: All historical data becomes invisible to queries (data appears to vanish!).\n\nHow `VACUUM FREEZE` Solves It:\nTo prevent wraparound, PostgreSQL assigns a special frozen transaction ID (`FrozenXID` = 2) to old tuples. By definition, `FrozenXID` is older than every normal XID.\n- `VACUUM (FREEZE)` scans heap pages, replacing old XIDs with `FrozenXID`.\n- Safety Mechanism: If the database approaches the 2-billion limit without vacuuming, PostgreSQL initiates an emergency aggressive autovacuum. If that fails, it shuts down the entire database and refuses to accept writes until vacuuming completes!",
    "bullet_points": [
      "32-bit XIDs wrap around after 4.29 billion transactions; modulo logic treats numbers older than 2.1B as future.",
      "Wraparound makes historical committed data vanish from query visibility.",
      "VACUUM FREEZE replaces old XIDs with FrozenXID to preserve visibility.",
      "Postgres will shut down and refuse writes if wraparound safety margins are breached."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "```sql\n-- Check age of oldest unfrozen XID across databases:\nSELECT datname, age(datfrozenxid) FROM pg_database ORDER BY age(datfrozenxid) DESC;\n\n-- If age exceeds 200,000,000 (autovacuum_freeze_max_age), emergency autovacuum triggers:\nVACUUM FREEZE ANALYZE critical_table;\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "PostgreSQL 17+ introduced 64-bit full transaction IDs internally (`FullTransactionId`) to permanently eliminate wraparound hazards for internal subsystems.",
    "company_tags": [
      "PostgreSQL Core",
      "Amazon",
      "Meta",
      "Uber"
    ],
