    "id": "int-dbms-074",
    "topic_id": "topic-dbms",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "DBMS",
    "subject_label": "DBMS",
    "title": "How do MySQL InnoDB Record Locks, Gap Locks, and Next-Key Locks prevent Phantom Reads under Repeatable Read?",
    "answer": "To eliminate Phantom Reads under `REPEATABLE READ`, MySQL InnoDB uses three interlocking lock types in its B+ tree index:\n\n1. Record Lock: Locks a specific existing index record (e.g., locking row where `id = 10`).\n2. Gap Lock: Locks the empty gap BETWEEN two index records, or the gap before the first or after the last record. It does not lock the record itself; it prevents other transactions from INSERTING new rows into that gap!\n3. Next-Key Lock: A combination of a Record Lock on the index record PLUS a Gap Lock on the gap immediately preceding that record: $(\\text{previous\\_key}, \\text{current\\_key}]$.\n\nExample:\nSuppose an index contains values: `[10, 20, 30]`.\n- Next-Key locks divide the key space into intervals:\n  - $(-\\infty, 10]$\n  - $(10, 20]$\n  - $(20, 30]$\n  - $(30, +\\infty)$\n- If Transaction 1 executes: `SELECT * FROM t WHERE id BETWEEN 15 AND 25 FOR UPDATE;`\n- InnoDB places Next-Key locks on $(10, 20]$ and $(20, 30]$.\n- If Transaction 2 attempts to `INSERT INTO t (id) VALUES (16);`, it BLOCKS on the gap lock $(10, 20]$!\n- Result: Zero phantom inserts allowed!",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Record Lock locks an existing index row.",
      "Gap Lock locks the space between records, blocking concurrent INSERTs.",
      "Next-Key Lock combines Record Lock + preceding Gap Lock: $(prev, current]$.",
      "Guarantees phantom read prevention in MySQL InnoDB under Repeatable Read."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "```sql\n-- Table with IDs: 10, 20, 30\n-- T1 executes locking range read:\nBEGIN;\nSELECT * FROM products WHERE price BETWEEN 10 AND 20 FOR UPDATE;\n-- Locks gap (0, 10], gap (10, 20], and gap (20, 30]!\n\n-- T2 attempts to insert a new product with price = 15:\nINSERT INTO products (price) VALUES (15);\n-- BLOCKS! Must wait until T1 commits! No phantom row created!\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "Gap locking is disabled under `READ COMMITTED` isolation level, which is why high-throughput MySQL architectures often switch from `REPEATABLE READ` to `READ COMMITTED`.",
    "company_tags": [
      "Amazon",
      "Uber",
      "MySQL Core",
      "Oracle"
    ],
    "frequency": "VERY_HIGH",
    "difficulty": "MEDIUM",
