    "id": "int-dbms-077",
    "topic_id": "topic-dbms",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "DBMS",
    "subject_label": "DBMS",
    "title": "How do Inverted Indexes power Full-Text Search engines (Elasticsearch, Lucene, PostgreSQL tsvector)?",
    "answer": "A standard forward database index maps `RowID -> Document Content`. Searching for a word requires scanning all rows ($O(N)$).\n\nAn Inverted Index flips the mapping: `Term (Word) -> List of Document IDs (Posting List)`.\n\nText Ingestion Pipeline:\n1. Tokenization: Splits raw text into words, removing punctuation.\n2. Normalization: Converts text to lowercase.\n3. Stopword Removal: Drops high-frequency, low-signal words (`a`, `the`, `is`, `on`).\n4. Stemming / Lemmatization: Reduces words to root base form (e.g., `running`, `runs`, `ran` $\\implies$ `run`) using algorithms like Porter Stemmer.\n5. Dictionary & Postings List: For each term, appends document ID, term frequency, and word position (for phrase queries).\n\nRelevance Scoring (BM25 / TF-IDF):\n- TF (Term Frequency): How often the term appears in this document.\n- IDF (Inverse Document Frequency): How rare the term is across the entire corpus.\n- Documents with rare terms matching frequently score highest.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Inverted index maps distinct terms to posting lists of matching document IDs.",
      "Preprocessing pipeline: Tokenization -> Lowercasing -> Stopwords -> Stemming.",
      "BM25 scoring combines Term Frequency and Inverse Document Frequency for relevance ranking."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "```sql\n-- Full-Text Search in PostgreSQL:\nCREATE TABLE articles (\n    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n    body TEXT,\n    tsv TSVECTOR GENERATED ALWAYS AS (to_tsvector('english', body)) STORED\n);\n\n-- Build GIN (Generalized Inverted Index) on the tsvector column:\nCREATE INDEX idx_articles_gin ON articles USING GIN (tsv);\n\n-- Query runs in O(log N) using inverted index match operator (@@):\nSELECT id FROM articles WHERE tsv @@ to_tsquery('english', 'database & performance');\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "In PostgreSQL, GIN (Generalized Inverted Index) is the standard inverted index implementation for full-text search and JSONB containment queries (`@>`).",
    "company_tags": [
      "Elasticsearch",
      "Google",
      "Amazon",
      "PostgreSQL Core"
    ],
    "frequency": "VERY_HIGH",
