    "id": "int-os-039",
    "topic_id": "topic-os",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "OPERATING_SYSTEMS",
    "subject_label": "Operating Systems",
    "title": "What is Belady's Anomaly in Page Replacement? Prove with an exact reference string that FIFO can cause MORE page faults with MORE physical frames.",
    "answer": "Intuition suggests that allocating more physical memory frames to a process should always decrease (or at least keep constant) the number of page faults.\n\nBelady's Anomaly (László Bélády, 1969):\nA counterintuitive phenomenon where increasing the number of page frames causes an INCREASE in the total number of page faults for certain page replacement algorithms (such as FIFO)!\n\nMathematical Proof using Reference String:\nReference string: `1, 2, 3, 4, 1, 2, 5, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5` (12 accesses)\n\nCase 1: 3 Page Frames with FIFO:\n- Page Faults = 9 faults!\n\nCase 2: 4 Page Frames with FIFO (More Memory!):\n- Access 1: [1, -, -, -] (Fault 1)\n- Access 2: [1, 2, -, -] (Fault 2)\n- Access 3: [1, 2, 3, -] (Fault 3)\n- Access 4: [1, 2, 3, 4] (Fault 4)\n- Access 1: [1, 2, 3, 4] (Hit)\n- Access 2: [1, 2, 3, 4] (Hit)\n- Access 5: Replaces 1 (oldest) -> [5, 2, 3, 4] (Fault 5)\n- Access 1: Replaces 2 (oldest) -> [5, 1, 3, 4] (Fault 6)\n- Access 2: Replaces 3 (oldest) -> [5, 1, 2, 4] (Fault 7)\n- Access 3: Replaces 4 (oldest) -> [5, 1, 2, 3] (Fault 8)\n- Access 4: Replaces 5 (oldest) -> [4, 1, 2, 3] (Fault 9)\n- Access 5: Replaces 1 (oldest) -> [4, 5, 2, 3] (Fault 10!)\n- Result: 10 page faults with 4 frames, compared to 9 faults with 3 frames!\n\nWhy It Occurs: Stack Algorithms vs Non-Stack Algorithms:\n- Stack Algorithms (LRU, Optimal) are mathematically immune to Belady's Anomaly because the set of pages in $n$ frames is always a subset of pages in $n+1$ frames ($S_n \\subset S_{n+1}$).\n- FIFO is NOT a stack algorithm.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Belady's Anomaly: Increasing frame allocation causes more page faults.",
      "Occurs in FIFO; proved with string `1, 2, 3, 4, 1, 2, 5, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5` (9 faults on 3 frames, 10 on 4 frames).",
      "Stack algorithms (LRU, Optimal) are mathematically immune to Belady's anomaly."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "c",
      "code": "```text\nBelady's Anomaly Summary:\nFrames: 3  ===>  9 Page Faults\nFrames: 4  ===> 10 Page Faults! (More RAM resulted in WORSE performance!)\nReason: FIFO ignores recency and frequency of access.\n```"
    },
    "pro_tip": "Interviewers frequently ask: 'Is LRU vulnerable to Belady's Anomaly?' The answer is categorically NO, because LRU satisfies the formal mathematical inclusion property of a Stack Algorithm.",
