    "id": "int-cn-066",
    "topic_id": "topic-cn",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "COMPUTER_NETWORKS",
    "subject_label": "Computer Networks",
    "title": "Explain Content Delivery Networks (CDNs): Edge Caching, Origin Shield, Cache Invalidation, and Geo-DNS vs Anycast.",
    "answer": "A Content Delivery Network (CDN) is a geographically distributed network of proxy edge servers that caches content close to end users, dramatically reducing latency and offloading origin web servers.\n\nCore CDN Architectural Concepts:\n1. Edge Caching & Point of Presence (POP):\nUsers fetch static assets (images, video, JS/CSS) and cached API responses from the nearest edge POP rather than traversing thousands of miles to a centralized origin datacenter.\n2. Origin Shield:\nA centralized intermediate caching tier placed between edge POPs and the origin server. If 200 edge POPs across the globe experience cache misses for the same asset simultaneously, they query the Origin Shield instead of pounding the origin server, preventing the 'Thundering Herd' origin crash.\n3. Cache Invalidation & Purging:\n- Time-to-Live (TTL): Content expires automatically.\n- Instant Purging: API calls evict specific URLs or cache tags (`Cache-Tag` / `Surrogate-Key`) from global edge caches in under 150 milliseconds.\n- Stale-While-Revalidate (`Cache-Control: max-age=600, stale-while-revalidate=30`): Serves stale cached content instantly to the user while fetching the updated version asynchronously in the background.\n\nRouting Traffic to the Nearest Edge:\n- Geo-DNS: The authoritative DNS server inspects the client resolver's IP address (or EDNS Client Subnet) and returns the IP of the physically closest edge datacenter.\n- Anycast BGP: The identical IP address is advertised globally by all POPs via BGP. Internet routers automatically route packets to the topologically closest edge POP with sub-millisecond route convergence.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "CDNs cache static and dynamic assets at edge POPs close to end users.",
      "Origin Shield acts as an intermediate cache protecting origin servers from global cache stampedes.",
      "`stale-while-revalidate` serves stale cache instantly while revalidating asynchronously in the background.",
      "Traffic is directed to edge POPs via Geo-DNS or Anycast BGP routing."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "bash",
      "code": "/* CDN Edge & Origin Shield Architecture */\n\n[ Client in London ] ---> [ London Edge POP ] ----\\\\\n[ Client in Paris  ] ---> [ Paris Edge POP  ] -----+---> [ Origin Shield ] ---> [ Origin Server ]\n[ Client in Berlin ] ---> [ Berlin Edge POP ] ----/      (Consolidates 200      (Protected from\n                                                          misses into 1!)        traffic storms)"
    },
    "pro_tip": "Surrogate Keys / Cache Tags are essential for enterprise CDN caching: e.g., an e-commerce product page tags its response with `Cache-Tag: product-1234, category-shoes`. When inventory updates, a single API purge call for `product-1234` evicts the product across all global edge servers instantly!",
