    "id": "int-sql-032",
    "topic_id": "topic-sql",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "SQL_QUERIES",
    "subject_label": "SQL Queries",
    "title": "Write a query to calculate Running Balance and Flag Overdraft Events for bank transactions.",
    "answer": "Financial ledgers record individual credit (+) and debit (-) transactions. An overdraft occurs when a transaction causes the account's running balance to drop below \\$0.00.\n\nSolution Steps:\n1. Translate transaction types into signed amounts: Credits are positive; Debits are negative.\n2. Compute the cumulative running balance using `SUM(signed_amount) OVER (PARTITION BY account_id ORDER BY transaction_date, id ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)`.\n3. Flag overdrafts where `running_balance < 0`.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Converts credits and debits into signed numerical values for mathematical accumulation.",
      "Calculates cumulative running balance using `SUM() OVER(PARTITION BY acc ORDER BY date)`.",
      "Tie-breaker: Orders by `trans_date, id` to enforce deterministic transaction sequencing.",
      "Flags overdraft events when `current_balance < 0` to apply financial penalty fees."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "/* Running Balance & Overdraft Detection */\n\nWITH NormalizedTransactions AS (\n    SELECT \n        id,\n        account_id,\n        trans_date,\n        amount,\n        CASE WHEN type = 'CREDIT' THEN amount ELSE -amount END AS signed_amount\n    FROM bank_ledger\n),\nRunningBalances AS (\n    SELECT \n        id,\n        account_id,\n        trans_date,\n        signed_amount,\n        -- Running balance calculation\n        SUM(signed_amount) OVER(\n            PARTITION BY account_id \n            ORDER BY trans_date, id \n            ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW\n        ) AS current_balance\n    FROM NormalizedTransactions\n)\nSELECT \n    id,\n    account_id,\n    trans_date,\n    signed_amount,\n    current_balance,\n    CASE WHEN current_balance < 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS is_overdraft,\n    -- Calculate overdraft penalty fee\n    CASE WHEN current_balance < 0 THEN 35.00 ELSE 0.00 END AS overdraft_fee\nFROM RunningBalances\nORDER BY account_id, trans_date;"
    },
    "pro_tip": "Notice the tie-breaker `ORDER BY trans_date, id`! If a customer deposits \\$100 and withdraws \\$50 on the exact same second, ordering by `id` ensures transactions process in the exact chronological ledger arrival order, preventing erroneous overdraft flags!",
    "company_tags": [
      "Stripe",
      "Goldman Sachs",
      "JPMorgan",
      "Coinbase"
    ],
    "frequency": "VERY_HIGH",
