    "id": "int-sql-040",
    "topic_id": "topic-sql",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "SQL_QUERIES",
    "subject_label": "SQL Queries",
    "title": "Write a query to find Second-Degree Friends (Friend-of-a-Friend Recommendations) in a Social Network.",
    "answer": "In a social graph table `friendships(user_id, friend_id)`, a second-degree friend is a 'friend of a friend' who is NOT already a direct first-degree friend of the user, and is not the user themselves.\n\nSolution Steps:\n1. Normalize Friendships (Make Bidirectional): If the table only stores `(A, B)` where $A < B$, union with `(B, A)` to make edges bidirectional.\n2. Self-Join: Join `User -> DirectFriend (f1)` to `DirectFriend -> FriendOfFriend (f2)` on `f1.friend_id = f2.user_id`.\n3. Filter Self: Ensure `f2.friend_id <> f1.user_id`.\n4. Filter Direct Friends: Ensure `f2.friend_id` is NOT already a 1st-degree friend using `NOT EXISTS`.\n5. Rank Recommendations: Group by `(user_id, recommended_friend)` and count mutual friends (`COUNT(*) AS mutual_friend_count`)!",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Normalizes undirected friendships into bidirectional edges via UNION.",
      "Self-joins 1st-degree edges to 2nd-degree edges on intermediate mutual friends.",
      "Uses `NOT EXISTS` to filter out users who are already direct 1st-degree friends.",
      "Orders recommendations by mutual friend count (`COUNT(*) DESC`)."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "/* Friend-of-a-Friend Recommendation Engine */\n\nWITH AllFriendships AS (\n    SELECT user_id, friend_id FROM friendships\n    UNION\n    SELECT friend_id AS user_id, user_id AS friend_id FROM friendships\n)\nSELECT \n    f1.user_id,\n    f2.friend_id AS recommended_friend,\n    COUNT(*) AS mutual_friends_count\nFROM AllFriendships f1\n-- Join to friends of friends\nJOIN AllFriendships f2 \n  ON f1.friend_id = f2.user_id\n-- Exclude self\nWHERE f2.friend_id <> f1.user_id\n-- Exclude existing direct 1st-degree friends!\n  AND NOT EXISTS (\n      SELECT 1 FROM AllFriendships direct \n      WHERE direct.user_id = f1.user_id \n        AND direct.friend_id = f2.friend_id\n  )\nGROUP BY f1.user_id, f2.friend_id\nORDER BY f1.user_id, mutual_friends_count DESC;"
    },
    "pro_tip": "This is the exact algorithm behind LinkedIn's 'People You May Know' and Facebook's friend recommendation engine. In massive production systems, this graph traversal is pre-calculated using distributed graph engines (Apache Giraph or Neo4j) and cached in Redis.",
