    "subject": "SQL_QUERIES",
    "subject_label": "SQL Queries",
    "title": "Explain Splay/Unnesting Arrays and JSON in SQL: UNNEST (Postgres) vs JSON_TABLE (MySQL/Oracle).",
    "answer": "Modern relational databases frequently store nested arrays and JSON documents. Unnesting expands a single row containing an array into multiple discrete rows (one per element):\n\n1. PostgreSQL: `UNNEST()` and `jsonb_array_elements()`:\n- Arrays: `SELECT id, UNNEST(tags) AS tag FROM articles;`\n- JSONB: `SELECT id, jsonb_array_elements_text(attributes->'colors') AS color FROM products;`\n- Preserving Array Index: `UNNEST(tags) WITH ORDINALITY AS t(tag, idx)` appends a 1-based index column.\n\n2. MySQL (8.0+) / Oracle: `JSON_TABLE()`:\nTransforms a JSON document into a relational table structure using JSONPath expressions directly inside the FROM clause.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Unnesting flattens nested arrays and JSON collections into relational row sets.",
      "PostgreSQL uses `UNNEST()` for arrays and `jsonb_array_elements()` for JSONB.",
      "`WITH ORDINALITY` tracks original array element index positions (1-indexed).",
      "MySQL 8+ and Oracle use `JSON_TABLE()` to project JSONPaths into relational columns."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "/* Unnesting Arrays & JSON */\n\n-- PostgreSQL Array Unnesting with Ordinality:\nSELECT \n    order_id,\n    item,\n    item_idx\nFROM customer_orders,\nUNNEST(items_array) WITH ORDINALITY AS t(item, item_idx);\n\n-- MySQL 8.0 JSON_TABLE() Unnesting:\nSELECT \n    p.id,\n    jt.color\nFROM products p,\nJSON_TABLE(\n    p.json_data,\n    '$.colors[*]' COLUMNS (\n        color VARCHAR(50) PATH '$'\n    )\n) AS jt;"
    },
    "pro_tip": "In PostgreSQL, use `CROSS JOIN LATERAL` when unnesting sub-elements dependent on outer row attributes to ensure the optimizer flattens queries efficiently!",
