    "id": "int-sql-078",
    "topic_id": "topic-sql",
    "category": "CORE_CS",
    "subject": "SQL_QUERIES",
    "subject_label": "SQL Queries",
    "title": "Sessionization of Event Clickstreams: Reconstructing User Sessions After 30-Minute Inactivity",
    "answer": "### The Sessionization Problem in Web Analytics\n\nWeb analytics platforms (Google Analytics, Mixpanel) record raw user clicks. A **Session** is defined as a cluster of events where no two consecutive events are separated by more than 30 minutes of inactivity. If a user idles for 30 minutes, the next event starts a brand new session.\n\n```\nEvent 1: 10:00 (Start Session 1)\nEvent 2: 10:15 (Delta = 15m <= 30m -> Same Session 1)\nEvent 3: 10:55 (Delta = 40m > 30m  -> START SESSION 2!)\nEvent 4: 11:05 (Delta = 10m <= 30m -> Same Session 2)\n```\n\n#### Step-by-Step SQL Resolution\n\n##### Step 1: Calculate Delta from Previous Event Using `LAG()`\nFlag any event where time elapsed exceeds 30 minutes (or the very first event) as a new session start (`1`), otherwise `0`.\n\n##### Step 2: Running Cumulative Sum of Session Starts\nA running `SUM()` over the binary flags produces a monotonically increasing session sequence ID!\n\n```sql\nWITH event_deltas AS (\n    SELECT \n        user_id,\n        event_time,\n        event_type,\n        -- Calculate time difference in seconds from prior event\n        EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (event_time - LAG(event_time) OVER (\n            PARTITION BY user_id \n            ORDER BY event_time\n        ))) AS seconds_since_last_event\n    FROM user_events\n),\nsession_flags AS (\n    SELECT \n        user_id,\n        event_time,\n        event_type,\n        -- If gap is NULL (first event) or > 1800s (30m), flag as 1\n        CASE \n            WHEN seconds_since_last_event IS NULL OR seconds_since_last_event > 1800 THEN 1 \n            ELSE 0 \n        END AS is_new_session\n    FROM event_deltas\n),\nsessionized_events AS (\n    SELECT \n        user_id,\n        event_time,\n        event_type,\n        -- Running sum generates unique session ID per user\n        SUM(is_new_session) OVER (\n            PARTITION BY user_id \n            ORDER BY event_time\n            ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW\n        ) AS session_seq\n    FROM session_flags\n)\nSELECT \n    user_id,\n    session_seq,\n    MIN(event_time) AS session_start,\n    MAX(event_time) AS session_end,\n    COUNT(*) AS total_clicks,\n    EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (MAX(event_time) - MIN(event_time))) / 60.0 AS session_duration_minutes\nFROM sessionized_events\nGROUP BY user_id, session_seq\nORDER BY user_id, session_start;\n```\n\n### Key Takeaways for Quick Revision\n- Sessionization is a classic variation of the **Gaps and Islands** pattern.\n- `LAG()` computes the timestamp delta against the prior click event.\n- Binary flag (`1` if `delta > threshold`, else `0`) marks session boundaries.\n- Running cumulative `SUM(flag)` assigns identical session IDs to all events within that cluster.\n\n> **Pro Tip / Interviewer Trap**:\n> Never use `AVG(session_duration)` without handling single-click bounces (`COUNT(*) = 1`)! For single-click sessions, `MAX(event_time) - MIN(event_time) = 0`, skewing average session duration downward.",
    "bullet_points": [
      "Sessionization is a classic variation of the **Gaps and Islands** pattern.",
      "`LAG()` computes the timestamp delta against the prior click event.",
      "Binary flag (`1` if `delta > threshold`, else `0`) marks session boundaries.",
      "Running cumulative `SUM(flag)` assigns identical session IDs to all events within that cluster."
    ],
    "code_snippet": {
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "-- Unique Global Session ID Generation (Combining User + Session Index):\nSELECT \n    user_id || '-' || session_seq AS session_token,\n    user_id,\n    MIN(event_time) AS session_started_at,\n    COUNT(*) AS page_views\nFROM sessionized_events\nGROUP BY user_id, session_seq;"
    },
    "pro_tip": "> Never use `AVG(session_duration)` without handling single-click bounces (`COUNT(*) = 1`)! For single-click sessions, `MAX(event_time) - MIN(event_time) = 0`, skewing average session duration downward.",
    "company_tags": [
      "Sessionization",
      "Window Functions",
      "Clickstream",
      "Analytics",
      "Gaps and Islands"
    ],
    "frequency": "VERY_HIGH",
