      "code": "-- Dynamic Identifier Whitelisting in PostgreSQL (Handling dynamic column/table names safely):\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION get_sorted_users(sort_col TEXT) \nRETURNS SETOF users LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $$\nBEGIN\n    -- Assert that input column is strictly an existing column in users table:\n    IF sort_col NOT IN ('id', 'username', 'created_at') THEN\n        RAISE EXCEPTION 'Invalid sort column: %', sort_col;\n    END IF;\n\n    -- quote_ident safely escapes verified identifiers:\n    RETURN QUERY EXECUTE format('SELECT * FROM users ORDER BY %I', sort_col);\nEND;\n$$;"
